# Codebase Atlas deployment

When asked to install, deploy, connect, update, verify, or remove Codebase
Atlas, follow `docs/CODEX_DEPLOYMENT_RULES.md`.

- Install end-user software only from the latest stable GitHub Release.
- Verify published checksums before installing or extracting assets.
- Reuse a valid versioned machine installation; create separate project config,
  identity and index data for every repository.
- Preview onboarding and Codex integration before applying them.
- Never copy development/evaluation paths, overwrite foreign configuration,
  modify target source, or silently change global MCP/editor settings.
- Require exact repository identity, `doctor=ready`, a fresh index and one real
  project query before reporting success.
